  work where we've previously helped  similar clients or  oh actually you know such and such i  help them you know worth asking them  um and then as part of my questioning  around their situation perhaps if they  are looking you get into team and  understanding what they've done to get  to that point  you can then you know just ask an honest  question you know an open question about  you know how they you know typically  would go about recruitment and  you know start that yeah i think  sometimes it's you can overthink those  questions but actually just asking that  question is  is the hardest is the hardest thing for  people to do and not enough people do it  um you know try and skirt around the  question trying cleverly about how i can  you know win this piece of work you know  by asking it as long as you build you  know as long as you build up some form  of credibility and  and hopefully by being engaging and  knowledgeable about your industry or  sector  by asking that question you shouldn't  get a negative response  i often find if you get a negative  response or closed or really you know  quite like why have you asked that you  know that you know that's not you know  that's not right or that's not what this  call is about then that's typically  because  we haven't done enough in the start to  build up  yeah we just haven't done enough to make  sure they know why um but hopefully if  you've done that bit right  that question yeah you might not  necessarily want but you probably get an  answer that you can then work with again  and then i guess it's about in your mind  working out when that next touch point  is and when that next conversation is  um yeah i don't you know i would never  expect to go into that call  um picking up and picking up a job i  would expect to go into that call  um knowing that i'm going to do my best  to you know give them a good impression  of me  so that if i pick up the phone again and  again and again hopefully over time i'll  win tha